---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import {sources,publication,evidence,url} from '../lib/content';
---
<Base title="Sources and provenance" description="Public primary references, private experimental provenance and the scope of the publication's MIT license."><div class="page-heading"><span class="section-number">THE REFERENCE SHELF</span><h1>Sources, not shortcuts.</h1><p>Public references explain the surrounding architecture. Local experiment records support the project's own observations. Their roles stay distinct.</p></div><section id="provenance" class="provenance-banner"><div><span class="section-number">EDITION {publication.edition} / {publication.date}</span><h2>A fixed research snapshot.</h2></div><div><p>The source corpus is pinned at <code class="long-hash">{publication.sourceRevision}</code>. Each of the {evidence.length} public evidence records identifies its reviewed private documents by basename and SHA-256.</p><p>The records combine editorial interpretation, captured values, selected original excerpts and reviewed images. Complete run artifacts and the implementation repository are not distributed, and independent public reproduction is not claimed. Basenames and digests preserve traceability for a future authorized review.</p></div></section><section class="source-shelf"><h2>Public references</h2><p class="muted">Pinned revisions are used where available. Living documentation may change. A source's role is stated below; an upstream report is not local validation.</p>{sources.map(s=><article class="source-entry" id={s.id}><span class="evidence-id">{s.id}</span><div><span class="mono">{s.kind}</span><h3><a href={s.url}>{s.title} ↗</a></h3><p>{s.scope}</p><a class="source-url" href={s.url}>{s.url}</a></div></article>)}</section><section class="prose license-note"><h2>License and attribution</h2><p>The original articles, original diagrams, curated data organization and website code are licensed under MIT. Linked documentation and source code retain their respective licenses. Depicted Apple interfaces in research captures retain their original rights; MIT does not relicense that third-party content. The physical photograph is a lossless screen crop, with source identity and crop bounds recorded in its evidence data. Apple and PINE64 names are used descriptively; this publication is independent of both organizations.</p><p>The interface uses locally served Schibsted Grotesk and IBM Plex Mono, under the SIL Open Font License. Font license texts are included in the repository and <a href={url('licenses/Schibsted-Grotesk-OFL.txt')}>here</a> and <a href={url('licenses/IBM-Plex-Mono-OFL.txt')}>here</a>. There is no analytics service, tracking script, advertising or remote AI endpoint.</p><p>Understand-Anything inspired the connected-concept and guided-reading organization. Its application code is not incorporated. Claude participated in editorial interface design and review; research claims were checked against the pinned project records.</p></section></Base>
